WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
Census day, 2011.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.110
Across England and Wales, people tick
boxes for their national identity.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:12.230
Well over half, 57.7 per
cent, tick English only.

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:18.060
Ten years later, at the 2021 census, the
English-only share has fallen to 14.9

5
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.110
per cent.

6
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:26.150
In a decade, the English-only count
fell from 32.4 million to 8.9 million.

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.330
Had people really changed?

8
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:33.090
In this mission, you'll see how schools,
sport and political parties build a sense

9
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.350
of nation.

10
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.590
Then you'll explore laws, landscapes,
and the four nations inside one state.

11
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.510
Your mission: find out whether millions
of people really stopped feeling English.
